  "notes": "Queensbridge reportage over jazz-loop minimalism. The distinguishing parameter is emptiness: the lowest melodic density on the boom-bap axis, because the harmony is implied by the sampled loop rather than written, and the beat is furniture the verse stands on. Premier's Illmatic-era drums are pitched down — a 100 BPM break dropped roughly 16 BPM — which is modelled as a slack quantize rather than as a tempo, since the engine has no sample to stretch. ⛔ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set, and it is a description rather than an exemption. The research is literal about this: *\"harmonic movement is implied by the sample, not written\"*. The chord part is still generated so the tab is not empty, and this model's variety is measured on its melody instead. ⚠ `snareRoll.pitchWalk` is inherited rather than authored: the research says nothing about how these producers pitch a roll, and lowering it was an invention that `drum_pitch.rs` correctly refused — a roll owes a producer three pitches unless the style is a train beat. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 45 to 44 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 45 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
